@startuml
title Launch Manager - Forced Run Target Activation

autonumber "<b>[00]"

participant "StateManager" as sm
participant "Launch Manager" as LM
participant "OS (kernel)" as kernel
participant "setup_filesystems.sh" as fs
participant "random" as ran
participant "app1" as app1

activate LM
activate sm

note over LM
Current Run Target: "Minimal"
Components StateManager and setup_filesystems.sh are Ready.
end note

sm -> LM : Activate Run Target ("Running", forced=False)
LM -> LM: validate Run Target "Running"
alt #White Run Target "Running" is valid
    LM -> LM: Queue Run Target Activation "Running"
    [<-- LM: Request accepted
else #Pink Run Target "Running" is invalid (Example: Run Target not configured)
    [<-- LM: Request rejected
end alt

sm -> LM : Activate Run Target ("Full", forced=False)
LM -> LM: validate Run Target "Full"
alt #White Run Target "Full" is valid
    LM -> LM: Queue Run Target Activation "Full"
    [<-- LM: Request accepted
else #Pink Run Target "Full" is invalid (Example: Run Target not configured)
    [<-- LM: Request rejected
end alt

note over LM
The following sequence assumes that both requests have been accepted.
end note

LM -> LM: Process next queued Run Target Activation: Run Target "Running"
LM -> LM: Determine transition plan from "Minimal" -> "Running"

group #White Start random
    LM -> kernel : Start random
    kernel -> ran ++ : Start random
    LM -> LM : Wait for random ready condition

    group #Yellow Forced Activation
        sm -> LM : Activate Run Target ("Off", forced=True)
        LM -> LM: validate Run Target "Off"
        alt  Run Target "Off" is valid
            [<-- LM: Request accepted
        else #Pink Run Target "Off" is invalid (Example: Run Target not configured)
            [<-- LM: Request rejected
        end alt
    end group

    note over LM
    The following sequence assumes that the "Off" request has been accepted.
    end note

    LM -> LM : Clear request queue (Removes "Full" from the queue).
    LM -> LM : Wait for ongoing operations to finish

    ran -> kernel : register /dev/random
    LM -> LM : Detect /dev/random exists, Component random Ready
end group

LM -> LM : Determine transition plan from current state to "Off"

note over LM
StateManager and random can be stopped in parallel as they do not depend on each other.
Component setup_filesystems must only be stopped after StateManager is stopped due to the dependency relationship.
end note

par Stop StateManager
    LM -> sm : SIGTERM
    alt StateManager terminates within the configured shutdown timeout
        sm -> sm : Terminate
        sm -> kernel : exit
        destroy sm
        kernel -> LM : StateManager terminated successfully
    else #pink StateManager does not terminate within the configured timeout
        LM -> sm : SIGKILL
        sm -> kernel : exit
        destroy sm
        kernel -> LM : StateManager terminated with error
    end alt
else Stop random
    LM -> ran : SIGTERM
    ran -> kernel : exit
    destroy ran
    kernel -> LM : random terminated successfully
end par

group #White Deactivate setup_filesystems.sh
    note over LM
        The underlying process is already in state terminated.
        Nothing to do.
    end note
    LM -> LM : Mark Component setup_filesystems.sh as Terminated
end group

LM -> LM: Run Target "Off" successfully activated

...
@enduml
